{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1126429-animal-purview-ape-human","id":1126429,"title":"Animal Purview (Ape)= Human?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-08T13:26:31-07:00","id":1126429,"title":"Animal Purview (Ape)= Human?","content":"I know this is a matter of viewpoint and is mainly anthropological in nature, but would you consider Animal purview (Ape) to include humans? Personally having taken several anthropology courses, I often think of humans as just a highly evolved ape species. I mean chimpanzee DNA is is only different from human by less than one percent. So personally I would include humans as a great ape. Would you consider this acceptable in your campaign? I would consider communication type boons to ensure a lack of mixed signals or misunderstandings, allowing the scion to communicate on a deeper intuitive level with human beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T14:10:38-07:00","id":1126445,"title":"","content":"Nah. There's no deity in any pantheon that wouldn't see a meaningful difference between apes and humans. The biggest Scion-esque mythological example of great apes I can think of is Hanuman's army in the Ramayana, and the ape warriors are clearly a different thing from humans, as well as a good target for a Purview in their own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T14:44:18-07:00","id":1126457,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it if you could describe a way to interact with human nature that was specific enough to the idea of humans as an animal species that it overlapped minimally with other Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T15:22:14-07:00","id":1126470,"title":"","content":"I would potentially allow a Scion intentionally pushing to build that sort of thing into their personal Legend to use Animal (Apes) to influence humans. However, that comes with two caveats. Firstly, just like Lula mentioned, I'd allow it to fiddle with the animal side of humans as long as it didn't start messing with other Purviews areas. Secondly, I wouldn't allow just anyone to use the Animal Purview to do this.<br /> <br /> Purviews don't deal with the scientific, exact thing. They are a bit more conceptual than that, and can get very culture-specific. The best example of this I think is darkness. Natural, scientific darkness from our reality, and the Darkness of the Divine of Scion are very different things. Darkness is almost tangible in myths, it almost has physical mass, and it exists independently of light. In our reality, darkness is an absence of light, where as in the reality of Scion, Darkness is something that can exist independently. A colossal snake embodying darkness can swallow the sun, night is draped like a blanket on the land, night is a horse, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> So, for most Pantheons (I don't know any Pantheon that made humanity out of apes, but there might be one somewhere) I would rule the Animal Purview doesn't effect humans. Humans, in their cosmology, are not related to apes. They are made of clay, ants, the bones of giants, and many other things. I <i>might</i> allow someone with an appropriate Purview mess with humans if they had an appropriate Purview and were somewhere where their Pantheon's cosmology was 'dominant,' like their Overworld, or somewhere on earth that is incredibly influenced by them. So, I might allow an Anunna God or Goddess fiddle with humans physical shape if they had the Earth Purview for example.<br /> <br /> If a Scion wanted to weave the modern, real-world concept of humans sharing a common ancestor with modern-day apes, become a Deity of Evolution, I would probably allow them to have a bit of a capacity to influence humans with the Animal Purview. I'd need them to establish it in-character though first, make it a part of their legend, weave it into their Pantheon's story. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Edit: I probably wouldn't allow Animal to influence languages or cultural things. It could do body language, but I put actual language as a technological development. Understanding humans doesn't let you understand the Hittites specifically, you just get the very simple, baseline of 'human,' without any of their cultural or technological developments. Thinking about this, it sounds a bit like the 'Wild' Purview the 2E Devs have been talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 08-08-2017, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T20:49:07-07:00","id":1126948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1126429-animal-purview-ape-human?p=1126445#post1126445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. There's no deity in any pantheon that wouldn't see a meaningful difference between apes and humans. The biggest Scion-esque mythological example of great apes I can think of is Hanuman's army in the Ramayana, and the ape warriors are clearly a different thing from humans, as well as a good target for a Purview in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Son Wukong also has a monkey army.<br /> <br /> <br /> And no, I would not say that Animal(Ape) allows you to effect humans. This is Sci-ON, not Sci-ENCE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:10:36-07:00","id":1127129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1126429-animal-purview-ape-human?p=1126445#post1126445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. There's no deity in any pantheon that wouldn't see a meaningful difference between apes and humans. The biggest Scion-esque mythological example of great apes I can think of is Hanuman's army in the Ramayana, and the ape warriors are clearly a different thing from humans, as well as a good target for a Purview in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, about that... the Vanaras may not be monkeys so much as they are a seperate race of beings with simian characteristics... if Animal/Beasts effects them then it should also effect Elves. (Now Hanuman as a God is associated with monkeys as his sacred animal, so he could still have that associated, but he's not a monkey himself, exactly).<br /> <br /> To quote the Ramayana :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When Vishnu attained the sonship of the great-souled king Dasharatha, then Brahma the self-created addressed all of the gods this way.<br /> <br /> &quot;Let mighty and guise changing helpmates be procreated to that truth abiding and valorous Vishnu who is the well-wisher of all of us.<br /> <br /> &quot;Let monkey-shaped progeny equalling Vishnu's valour be procreated from the physiques of prominent apsara-s and gandharva-s, from the girls of yaksha-s and pannaga-s, and also thus from the bodies of kinnaraa-s, she-vidyaadharaa-s, she-riksha-s and she-monkeys, and they shall be wizards of miracles and audacious ones, in travel they shall have air's speed, bestowed with intellect they shall be the knowers of ideation, and with their divine physique they shall be ineliminable, they shall be endowed with all the assaultive aspects of all missiles, and they shall be untiring in their efforts, like you who thrive on amrita, the ambrosia, unmindful of thirst and hunger.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have already created the eminent bear Jambavanta in earlier times, as he came forth from my yawning face. (i.e, use my Avatar Jambavan as a template for your own)<br /> <br /> When Brahma addressed them thus, those gods have agreed to his order and accordingly started to parent sons in the <i>semblance of monkeys</i>. </div> </div> </div>Note that it specifically says, semblance of monkeys, not monkeys... further along in the same chapter, we find that these Vanaras were born from all manner of beings:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thus the gods have procreated many thousands of such valorous and guise changing monkeys who with their immeasurable strength and bravery are manifest for the elimination of the decahedral demon Ravana.<br /> <br /> And they with their elephantine, mountainous and prodigious bodies quickly took birth in bears, monkeys, sacred langoors.<br /> <br /> Those that are procreated have attained the shape, getup and valour of the god that has fathered them, and thus the monkey race is procreated separately and individually.<br /> <br /> Some of the vanara-s endowed with superior valour are born to female langoors, and like that some more to female bears and kinnaraa-s.<br /> <br /> Several of the gods, great-sages, gandharva-s, eagles, yaksha-s, and the celebrated reptiles, kimpusha-s, siddha-s, vidyaadharaa-s, uraga-s and caarana-s and even the prominent maidens of apsara-s, she-vidyaadharaa-s, naaga, gandharva-s then gladly procreated all of the thousands of forest-ranging and valiant vanara sons from their bodies that are forest rangers. (The word vanara means, he who ranges through the vana, forests) </div> </div> </div>So yeah, Vanaras are as much monkeys as Sirens are birds, and I don't think they themselves would be covered by the Beasts Purview... they're also all Scions, or at least Incarnations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 08-10-2017, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T11:55:07-07:00","id":1127227,"title":"","content":"Science is really interesting in Scion. The biggest thing you need to do is sit down with your storyteller and figure out how their cosmology works. Some believe that all myths are true. Others pick and choose between primary myths, and select others to be nothing more than stories or misunderstandings. A few change their cosmology between every game just to mix things up and explore new and interesting stories.<br /> <br /> Once you figure out the general idea behind cosmology in your particular game, you can talk with your storyteller about how you want to play a scientist character. Discuss the kinds of mysteries you want to answer. Science is the systematic study of the structure and behavior of the physical and natural world through observation and experimentation. So what happens when your pantheon (for example) created Humanity out of Clay, and they can objectively prove it to you? In this version, Humanity has more in common with the Earth purview than Animal (Apes).<br /> <br /> But better yet, what does your scientist conclude when they stand before the gods of a different pantheon and they create Humanity by bleeding upon some ground up bones? What happens when your scientist is given two conflicting stories that can both be proven? Does your scientist settle upon the answer being subjective reality warping? Or is there some other, greater, hidden universal truth that your storyteller has placed into the setting for your scientist to discover?<br /> <br /> Science can be a lot of fun in Scion, but it often takes you places you never expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T14:35:52-07:00","id":1127333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1126429-animal-purview-ape-human?p=1126445#post1126445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah. There's no deity in any pantheon that wouldn't see a meaningful difference between apes and humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of an exception - the Supplemental Scions book included one entity by the name of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babi_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">Babi</a>.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't recommend incorporating this into the Animal purview, but this could be an interesting starting point for discussion at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T23:16:20-07:00","id":1127501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1126429-animal-purview-ape-human#post1126429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is a matter of viewpoint and is mainly anthropological in nature, but would you consider Animal purview (Ape) to include humans? Personally having taken several anthropology courses, I often think of humans as just a highly evolved ape species. I mean chimpanzee DNA is is only different from human by less than one percent. So personally I would include humans as a great ape. Would you consider this acceptable in your campaign? I would consider communication type boons to ensure a lack of mixed signals or misunderstandings, allowing the scion to communicate on a deeper intuitive level with human beings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Scientifically speaking, it might be possible. But you're dealing with a game centered around mythology; in which case, the process of natural evolution is questionable when there are various gods and goddesses attributed with having directly created humans (and other life forms) in their current states.<br /> <br /> As Watcher pointed out, there are many legends which say humans were created from other things besides apes. One could argue that the Earth purview would allow you to create and control human beings, As could most of the other purviews dealing with physical matter.<br /> <br /> In the real world, we tend to chalk mythology up to being allegory and metaphor, but in the world of Scion, mythology is taken in a very literal sense. Meaning it's difficult to tell what can and can't happen when it comes to supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1126429-animal-purview-ape-human?p=1126948#post1126948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Son Wukong also has a monkey army.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An army of DEMON monkeys, if I'm not mistaken?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1126429-animal-purview-ape-human?p=1127227#post1127227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science is really interesting in Scion. The biggest thing you need to do is sit down with your storyteller and figure out how their cosmology works. Some believe that all myths are true. Others pick and choose between primary myths, and select others to be nothing more than stories or misunderstandings. A few change their cosmology between every game just to mix things up and explore new and interesting stories.<br /> <br /> Once you figure out the general idea behind cosmology in your particular game, you can talk with your storyteller about how you want to play a scientist character. Discuss the kinds of mysteries you want to answer. Science is the systematic study of the structure and behavior of the physical and natural world through observation and experimentation. So what happens when your pantheon (for example) created Humanity out of Clay, and they can objectively prove it to you? In this version, Humanity has more in common with the Earth purview than Animal (Apes).<br /> <br /> But better yet, what does your scientist conclude when they stand before the gods of a different pantheon and they create Humanity by bleeding upon some ground up bones? What happens when your scientist is given two conflicting stories that can both be proven? Does your scientist settle upon the answer being subjective reality warping? Or is there some other, greater, hidden universal truth that your storyteller has placed into the setting for your scientist to discover?<br /> <br /> Science can be a lot of fun in Scion, but it often takes you places you never expected.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I've got an idea about that: What if the conflicting stories regarding how humans were created are about how the pantheons created their <b>specific groups </b>of people? In that scenario, you could explain why humans exist in so many different ethnic groups, because different pantheons went about it in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-11-2017, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}